health check:http://localhost:8000/health
docs: http://localhost:8000/docs

When container is running to see the logs we can run in separate powershell: docker logs -f medical-api

or the same we can see in LOgs in Docker Desktop


Open a shell inside the running container:

and we can ispect dependency: python -m pip list
or check: python -m pip check

To exit from docker: exit or docker exec

Test the API inside the container:
docker exec medical-api python -c "import urllib.request; print(urllib.request.urlopen('http://127.0.0.1:8000/health').read().decode())"

and we will see the repsonse from health: {"status": "healthy"}

Port mapping(can be used when internal request works but from windows or browser fails):
docker port medical-api

To start the Docker and get inside imidetly:
docker run --rm -it --entrypoint sh medical-api:1.0.0

Use -d to run the container in the background:
check docker ps -a  - check if there stopped containers and remove them
docker rm medical-api  - remove container
docker run -d --name medical-api -p 8000:8000 medical-api:1.0.0 - run in detach mode

Verify that the application is not running as root:
docker exec medical-api whoami - should be appuser

connnect to detached container:
docker exec -it medical-api sh

docker stop medical-api
docker rm medical-api

